==Bugs==
{{Bug|When using Whirlwind Sprint in certain ruins and dungeons, it is possible to clip through a stationary object and become trapped behind it. For instance, using Whirlwind Sprint near a bookshelf or cupboard will cause you to travel behind it and be unable to move out of that location.|confirmed=1}}
**{{pc22}}Using the console command <code>tcl</code> will allow you to move back into the movable area.
{{Bug|Sometimes when this shout is used, the sound effect of your character shouting will be delayed until you finish dashing.|confirmed=1}}
{{Bug|If you are over-encumbered and have a weapon equipped and sheathed, using Whirlwind Sprint while in third-person mode and immediately unsheathing your weapon will cause you to move extremely fast for a short time in whatever direction you are facing while shouting. This may drop your frame rate on low-end systems as you travel a great distance. (This bug also works while not over-encumbered but the effect is not nearly as pronounced nor as long-lasting.)|confirmed=1}}
{{Bug|While in third person view, you can use Whirlwind Sprint and jump while the effect of the shout is active (while you are being propelled forward). This will cause the above bug to occur, making your character travel a greater distance than what the shout would allow you to, at a great but slowly decreasing speed. The extra distance traveled, as well as the speed that this happens, is analogous to how many words have been used in the shout. However, in order for this bug to occur, your character must have contact with the ground the moment you jump. This is best achieved in slightly uphill surfaces. Perfectly flat surfaces will prevent the bug from occurring.|confirmed=1}}
{{Bug|If you jump while still being propelled forward by the shout and just before stepping on the first step of a staircase (for example the large staircase in [[Lore:Whiterun|Whiterun]] connecting the market area with the plateau the tree [[Lore:Gildergreen|Gildergreen]] is located), your character will perform an ultra powerful jump, reaching a great height.|confirmed=1}}
{{Bug|After learning the first word of this shout from the Greybeards, but ''before'' they bow and give you the knowledge to use it, you can enter the menu and unlock it yourself with one of your own dragon souls. If you do this, the second word will be prematurely unlocked once you do absorb their knowledge. If you already have the first word unlocked before meeting the Greybeards, this glitch can be used to prematurely unlock the third and final word instead.|confirmed=1}}
{{Bug|If you use the [[Skyrim:Controls#General_Gameplay|Wait]] function during the dash of Whirlwind Sprint, then spam the shout key, you will repeatedly dash for as many times as the key is mashed, even if you crash into a wall. The glitch will fail if you lose contact with the ground. If you use [[Skyrim:Waterwalking|waterwalking]], this can be used to quickly traverse large bodies of water.|confirmed=0}}
{{Bug|When learning the second word of Whirlwind Sprint - "Nah/Fury" - a separate version of the shout will appear in the Shouts menu. Each word of this separate shout will have 0 set as their cooldown time; this bug shares some similarity with the one that affects the Marked for Death shout, but it is currently unknown what causes this specific bug to occur.}}

